{
 "$comment": "AEP-0002 Annex A machine-usable mapping fixture for the OpenHands agent-server table, verified against OpenHands/software-agent-sdk @ cf6c2a3a (release v1.35.0; PyPI openhands-agent-server 1.35.0). Inputs are TRANSPORT-shaped (event_transport_dump: exclude_none, parent_id STRIPPED, legacy-filtered tools) \u2014 never raw SDK dumps; drift at a future pin is a re-verify, not a surprise. Each entry pins mapEvent at the bridge default posture (capture metadata, deltas OFF); entries whose behavior forks under the AEP_OPENHANDS_DELTAS opt-in carry deltas_expected (TokenEvent pins its refusal: nothing even under the opt-in - raw token-id planes are not observability). expected is {type, data, subject, step}. status_transitions pins the pure statusMoments table behind run synthesis and the attention moments (the server's own ConversationExecutionStatus enum; paused/waiting never close; running->idle closes honestly with reason=idle; attention.requested carries NO options and NO respond path - the read-only channel). Two registry-forced rules recorded in the design record banner: vendor types carry two segments after the token (x.openhands.<family>.<leaf>, mechanical from the kind), and a USER rejection is a human decision, not a policy block - rejection_source=hook maps to tool.denied by=policy while rejection_source=user stays vendor-scoped (x.openhands.user_reject.observation) with the attention.resolved event carrying the human moment. The naive server-local vendor timestamp and the vendor event id (the dedupe key) ride at metadata (vendor_ts / vendor_event_id); the envelope ts is bridge receive time. Runtime wiring (conversation_id scoping, socket replay + dedupe, the never-send auth-frame-only posture) is receiver state, smoke-pinned in the reference repository.",
 "identity": {
  "session_from": "conversation_id (the WebSocket path / REST discovery id; the socket scopes its events)",
  "run_from": "synthesized from ConversationStateUpdateEvent execution_status transitions (statusMoments)",
  "$comment": "The envelope step is stamped from llm_response_id on action/message events \u2014 a grouping fact, not a synthesized boundary. Vendor event id + naive server-local timestamp ride at metadata (vendor_event_id / vendor_ts); the envelope ts is bridge receive time."
 },
